From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:45:47 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/72] deepseek: apply shared lane grammar masks before
 selection

Carry prompt and verification masks through the native lane backend to each rank before greedy or keyed selection. Keep matching, draft cuts and scheduling in shared lanes, and release mask ownership after a successful drain.

Register the PTX launch with the kernel contract and derive contract image names from the build definitions. Host tests exercise masked first tokens, accepted draft prefixes, nonfinite logits, guards and corruption controls. Full CPU gates pass with zero new lean identities against 0d51120a8; device execution remains unqualified.
